  "releaseNotes": "### Smaller responses for external MCP agents\n\n- Connecting to a Pudding conversation now lists available tool names. Agents can look up the schema and instructions for a particular tool when they need them.\n- Pudding reuses unchanged project and skill instructions within a connection. Agents can request them again after losing context.\n- File searches and long command logs return previews with a way to read the original result. Browser tab snapshots omit embedded icon data and keep screenshots available.\n\n### Windows Store updates\n\n- When you choose to install a downloaded update, Pudding checks for active tasks. If Windows allows silent installation, the update proceeds without a confirmation dialog. Otherwise, Windows asks you to confirm.",
